Release the RM API lock in rm_power_source_change_event even when no GPU is
attached yet. Backport of NVIDIA's own fix, which first shipped in 615.78.08.

The _PSR (AC adapter) ACPI notifier is installed when nvidia.ko loads, before
RmInitAdapter attaches GPU 0. An AC power-source event in that window takes the
API lock, finds gpumgrGetGpu(0) == NULL, and returns without releasing it. GSP
init (kgspInitRm -> rmapiLockAcquire) and every later NVPCF notify then block
forever. See NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules#1421.

--- a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/osapi.c
@@ -4543,9 +4543,9 @@
                 }
                 os_unref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE);
             }
-            // UNLOCK: release API lock
-            rmapiLockRelease();
         }
+        // UNLOCK: release API lock
+        rmapiLockRelease();
     }
 
     if (rmStatus != NV_OK)
